{{Term/Store|Fruit|Fruits|Series, ALttP, LA, OoA, OoS, TWW, TP, ALBW, TFH, BotW, TotK, FPTRR, LCT, AoC, AoI|plural}} are a recurring class of [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= E |publisher= |page= 74}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Palm Fruit}}<br/>Fruit from palm trees that grow near the ocean. It doesn't offer any special effects but will increase your heart recovery when used as an ingredient.|Inventory|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|I hear that members of the {{Color TotK|Red|Yiga Clan}} have been camouflaging amid {{Color TotK|Red|fruit}}.|Lukan|TotK}}</ref><ref name="AoI Materials"/>{{Name Ref|AoC}}

==Location and Uses==
==={{ALttP|-}}===
{{Main|Apple}}

[[Link]] can obtain [[Apple]]s by dashing into [[Tree]]s with the [[Pegasus Shoes]]. They can be eaten to restore [[Heart]]s.

==={{LA|-}}===
{{Main|Apple, Banana, Cactus, Green Apple, Pineapple, Pumpkin}}
In {{LA}}, [[Apple]]s can be found in several [[Tree]]s around [[Koholint Island]], by eating them, Link can refill his [[Life Gauge]]. A cluster of [[Banana]]s and a [[Pineapple]] are used in the [[Trading Quest]]. A [[Monkey]] is seen throwing coconuts on [[Toronbo Shores]]. [[Cactus|Cacti]] appear as static enemies that damage Link if he walks into them, as [[Pokey]]s, and in some Houses as potted [[Plant]]s. Additionally, oranges and green [[Pumpkin]]s can be found in the [[Quadruplets House]].

